  ('ford-ranger-2026-50my-xl-single-cab-cc-3', 'Ford', 'Ranger', 2026, NULL, 'XL', 'single_cab', 'cab_chassis', 'full-time 4x4', '3.0L V6 turbo-diesel', '10-speed automatic', NULL, 'Standard light-vehicle licence subject to final configuration', 3270, 1925, 'Ford ''Kerb Weight'': full tank of fuel, no occupants, luggage or cargo, and the lightest possible orderable combination of factory-fit equipment; cab-chassis figures exclude tray bodies.', 3230, 6400, 1490, 1959, 1305, 'manufacturer-calculated GVM minus Ford Kerb Weight', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ford-ranger-2026-50my-au', 'Official 2026.50MY Ranger brochure, PDF p.8, table “4x4 | XL Ranger 2026.50MY Specifications”, row group “Vehicle Masses (kg)”; kerb/payload basis in footnote on the same page.', 'needs_secondary_review', 0, 'OPTIMISTIC KERB: stored kerb mass is the lightest-orderable-equipment figure, giving the largest payload. The 2026.50MY brochure was read in full on 4 September 2026 and publishes no heavier figure: pages 17 and 21 each carry a single Kerb Weight row, footnoted as the lightest possible orderable combination of factory fit equipment. Every stored GVM and kerb mass was re-checked against it and matched. There is no conservative figure to add from this source, so this disclosure is permanent unless Ford publishes one. Published on the owner''s decision as a guide, with the basis disclosed to the customer on the calculator: Beyond RV weighs the vehicle at the factory before build and those figures decide. Replace with the heavier options figure from the 2026.50MY brochure, page 21, when a copy is to hand. Not independently verified; ford.com.au blocks automated retrieval. Manufacturer derives payload by subtracting kerb mass from GVM. Ford warns that figures are approximate and subject to individual variance; weigh the actual vehicle. Cab-chassis kerb and payload exclude tray bodies.'),
