sis kerb and payload exclude tray bodies.'),
  ('kgm-musso-my26-elx-double-cab-tub', 'KGM', 'Musso', 2026, NULL, 'ELX', 'double_cab', 'pickup_tub', 'part-time 4WD with selectable low range and auto-locking rear differential', '2.2L turbo-diesel, 133 kW / 400 Nm', '6-speed automatic', NULL, 'Standard light-vehicle licence subject to final configuration', 3100, 2090, 'manufacturer-published kerb weight; no further kerb definition visible in the opened specification sheet', 2880, 6380, NULL, NULL, 790, 'manufacturer-published payload; derivation method not stated', 3500, 350, 1300, 1570, NULL, 'kgm-musso-my26-au', 'Official “MUSSO MY26 Technical Specifications & Features”, PDF p.1 of 3, table sections “Dimensions” and “Weights and Capacities”, Musso/Musso XLV and ELX/ADVANCE/ULTIMATE columns. Grade mapping cross-checked against the live Australian Musso page payload statement.', 'source_verified', 0, 'Tub-compatible camper only unless engineered tray conversion is verified. The live page uses “Adventure” once in the payload sentence, while its grade card and the official PDF use “Advance”. The 1,010 kg configuration maps to ELX XLV; the 880 kg configuration maps to Advance XLV and Ultimate XLV. No grade mapping was guessed.'),
