-- Mercedes-Benz Sprinter VS30 cab chassis, read from the Australian technical
-- brochure (MY25/MY26, issued April 2026) supplied by the owner on 4 September
-- 2026. Every row reconciles: GVM minus unladen mass equals the published payload.
--
-- Only the 5.0 and 5.5 tonne variants are here. The 4.49 tonne versions of the same
-- models sit under this table's CHECK (gvm_kg > 4500) and are deliberately left out
-- rather than widening the constraint: 517 MWB, 519 MWB, 519 MWB A4M, 517 LWB, 519 LWB, 519 LWB A4M, 519 MWB Dual, 519 LWB Dual, 519 LWB Dual A4M.
   'Sprinter and eSprinter Technical Data: Panel Van, Cab Chassis, Dual Cab Chassis and Transfer Minibus (VS30, MY25/MY26)',
   'https://www.mercedes-benz.com.au/content/dam/australia/vans/brochures-and-specifications/sprinter-panel-van/Sprinter%20VS30%20MY25%20MY26%20AU%20Tech%20Brochure%20April%202026%2020260326%20NEW.pdf',
   '2026-04', '2026-09-04', 'manufacturer_pdf', 'AU',
   'Effective July 2025 production, issued April 2026, footer states Model Year 2025. Cab chassis data on pages 23 to 26. Pages 25 and 26 label the body style row RWD Single Cab Chassis while the page title and the 9072 model type codes say Dual Cab Chassis; the title is correct.');

  id, make, model, model_year_start, model_year_end, variant, cab_type, axle_configuration, drivetrain,
